The issue is `.test` is a plain CSS class, not a Tailwind utility — variants like `md:` only work on utilities Tailwind knows about. Define it with the `@utility` directive instead so it becomes a real utility that supports variants:

```css
/* globals.css */
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```

Then `md:test` will work. (src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx, "Adding custom utilities" section, ~line 402-424)

